Construction BIM for ERPNext

This project builds on the architecture and approach of OpenConstructionERP
(https://openconstruction.org), AGPL-3.0 licensed — specifically its `bim_hub`
and `takeoff` modules, which this app ports into Frappe idioms.

OpenConstructionERP © its contributors. Where OCEP's open source delivers box
placeholders in its text fallback, the geometry reconstruction in this project
is original code (ifc_geometry.py) that extracts real vertices from the IFC
file directly; the closed DDC cad2data binary referenced by OCEP is NOT used.

Test IFC/PDF assets used during development:
"BIM4LCA" downloads from Nordic Sustainable Construction
(https://www.nordicsustainableconstruction.com/knowledge/2024/august/bim4lca-files)
— CC BY-SA 4.0, published 14-08-2024, WP1 Life Cycle Assessments. Design team:
Huvila Oy.

The three.js / GLTFLoader libraries bundled in public/js/three are vendored
under their respective MIT-style licenses (three.js is MIT).

Bundled dependencies under `construction_bim/public/js/`:
- `webifc/` (web-ifc 0.0.77, https://github.com/ThatOpen/engine_web-ifc) —
  **MPL-2.0**. Files: web-ifc.wasm, web-ifc-mt.wasm, IFCWorker.js,
  webifc-api-iife.js. MPL-2.0 allows combination into a larger work (this
  AGPL-3.0 app) without relicensing the app; the MPL-covered files themselves
  remain under MPL-2.0, and their source is available from the upstream
  repository above at the version listed.
- `webifc.bundle.js` is built from `frontend_src/webifc_build/entry2.js`
  (builder: esbuild, MIT). Regenerate with `frontend_src/webifc_build/build2.js`
  (requires `npm install` in that folder).
